78. Rename
    mv <filename> <new_filename> used to move/rename a file to the new name
        eg to rename roboto.font to roboto.woff: mv roboto.font roboto.woff


85. Move
     mv <file> <destination> used to move a file from current folder to new sub folder
    **Can also mv file based on path to another folder **
        How?
        Find -name <filename>
        mv <folder>/<filename> <destination path separated by "/")
86. Find
 -> ##Use find to find things or view a file tree of a folder; see all the files and subfolders wothin a folder
 -> find <folder name> used to displaty the file tree of a different folder in the current directory   
87. Move + Make Directory 
    mkdir client/<new_folder_name> used to make a subfolder in a directory without leaving the current directory
    mkdir <subfolder>/<another sub folder> without leaving "."
    mv <file> <subfolder>/<subfolder> only copies the file from one folder to another without using the "rm" command to delete it from the original folder


90. Find Subfolder
    find -name <subfolder name>

